{"pull": {"id": "number:23478", "number": 23478, "title": "KAFKA-21106: Fix ShareCompletedFetch leak when merging two fetches for the same partition", "state": "closed", "draft": false, "created_at": "2026-09-16T13:30:28Z", "closed_at": "2026-09-18T13:47:26Z", "merged_at": null, "user": {"login": "apoorvmittal10", "id": 2861565, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjE1NjU=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2861565?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10", "html_url": "https://github.com/apoorvmittal10", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "ShareInFlightBatch.merge() copied the absorbed batch's records into the\nlatest fetch batch but never cleared previous batch records, so the\nabsorbed ShareCompletedFetch looked permanently unacknowledged and\nleaked in ShareFetchBuffer.pendingAcknowledgementFetches. This merge can\nhappen whenever two completed fetches for the same partition are\ncollected together.\n\nReviewers: Shivsundar R <shr@confluent.io>, Omnia Ibrahim <o.g.h.ibrahim@gmail.com>, Andrew Schofield <aschofield@confluent.io>\n", "labels": [{"id": 7522931565, "node_id": "LA_kwDOACG9q88AAAABwGbTbQ", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/kafka/labels/ci-approved", "name": "ci-app